\image(figures/apriori_levels.svg)
// result_end

\caption(Candidates at each itemset size for minimum support 45 (5%): produced by the join (grey), left after pruning and counted (light blue), and frequent (dark blue).)
\alttext(Grouped bar chart over itemset sizes 1 to 6. Joined, counted and frequent counts: size 1, 15, 15, 15; size 2, 105, 105, 76; size 3, 272, 189, 135; size 4, 239, 127, 84; size 5, 61, 25, 21; size 6, 5, 2, 2.)

At 5% support the join produced 697 candidates over all levels. Pruning
removed 234 of them before any counting, and 463 were counted to find 333
frequent itemsets. Most of the work happens at sizes 3 and 4. At size 2
nothing can be pruned, since every single item is frequent, and all
\(\binom{15}{2}=105\) pairs are counted. Twelve of them can never occur,
such as \(\{\)`Sex=male`, `Sex=female`\(\}\), because each attribute takes
one value per passenger. Counting such pairs once is cheap, and since they
fail, the prune step removes every larger set that contains them. Each
passenger holds one value of each of six attributes, so at most
\(4\cdot3\cdot4\cdot3\cdot4\cdot3-1=1\,727\) itemsets are possible, out of
\(2^{15}\) subsets of the items. Apriori counted 463 of them. Raising the
support to 10% or 20% shrinks every level. Eclat and FP-growth agree with
Apriori at every threshold.

> Rules about survival

From the 333 frequent sets at 5% support, the block keeps the rules whose
consequent is a single `Survived` item and whose confidence is at least
0.8. For each rule it also computes:

- Fisher's exact test of independence between \(A\) and \(C\). The 2×2
  table has cells \(s(A\cup C)\), \(s(A)-s(A\cup C)\),
  \(s(C)-s(A\cup C)\) and \(N-s(A)-s(C)+s(A\cup C)\). The p-values are
  adjusted for multiple testing by Benjamini-Hochberg.
- The *improvement* (`rule_improvements`): the rule's confidence minus the
  best confidence of any rule with a strictly smaller antecedent and the
  same consequent. The empty antecedent has confidence equal to the base
  rate.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/apriori_rules.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

namespace alg = dm::algorithms;

int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto passengers = dm::datasets::titanic()
      | dm::mutate("Survived", [](const auto& r) { return std::string(r.get_double("Survived") > 0 ? "yes" : "no"); })
      | dm::mutate("Age", [](const auto& r) {
          return std::string(r.is_null("Age") ? "unknown" : r.get_double("Age") < 18 ? "child" : "adult"); })
      | dm::mutate("Family", [](const auto& r) {
          return std::string(r.get_double("SibSp") + r.get_double("Parch") > 0 ? "with" : "alone"); });
  const auto enc = alg::encode_transactions(passengers, {"Pclass", "Sex", "Age", "Family", "Embarked", "Survived"});
  const std::size_t N = enc.transactions.size();
  const auto frequent = alg::apriori_frequent_itemsets(enc.transactions, 45);
  const auto all_rules = alg::association_rules(frequent, N, 0.8);

  std::vector<alg::AssociationRule> rules;
  for (const auto& r : all_rules)
    if (r.consequent.size() == 1 && enc.labels[r.consequent[0]].starts_with("Survived")) rules.push_back(r);
  const auto improvement = alg::rule_improvements(rules, frequent, N);
  std::map<std::vector<std::size_t>, std::size_t> support;
  for (const auto& f : frequent) support[f.items] = f.support;
  std::vector<double> p;
  for (const auto& r : rules) {
    const std::size_t a = r.support, sa = support[r.antecedent], sc = support[r.consequent];
    p.push_back(dm::stats::fisher_exact_test_2x2(a, sa - a, sc - a, N - sa - sc + a).p_value);
  }
  const auto q = dm::stats::p_adjust(p, dm::stats::PAdjustMethod::BH);

  std::size_t significant = 0, improving = 0;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < rules.size(); ++i) {
    significant += q[i] < 0.05;
    improving += improvement[i] >= 0.02;
  }
  std::print("{} rules in all at confidence >= 0.8; {} have a single Survived consequent.\n"
             "{} have BH-adjusted Fisher p < 0.05; {} improve on every shorter rule by at least 0.02.\n\n",
             all_rules.size(), rules.size(), significant, improving);
  std::print("| rule | support | confidence | lift | improvement | adjusted p |\n"
             "| :--- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < rules.size(); ++i)
    if (improvement[i] >= 0.02)
      std::print("| {} => {} | {} | {:.3f} | {:.2f} | {:+.3f} | {:.1e} |\n",
                 alg::itemset_label(rules[i].antecedent, enc.labels),
                 alg::itemset_label(rules[i].consequent, enc.labels), rules[i].support, rules[i].confidence,
                 rules[i].lift, improvement[i], q[i]);

  std::vector<double> sx, sy;
  std::vector<dm::RGB> colour;
  for (std::size_t i = 0; i < all_rules.size(); ++i) {
    sx.push_back(static_cast<double>(all_rules[i].support) / N);
    sy.push_back(all_rules[i].confidence);
    const double t = std::clamp((all_rules[i].lift - 1.0) / 1.6, 0.0, 1.0);
    colour.push_back(dm::RGB{static_cast<std::uint8_t>(203 - 166 * t), static_cast<std::uint8_t>(213 - 114 * t),
                             static_cast<std::uint8_t>(225 + 10 * t)});
  }
  dm::graphics::RPlot::create()
      .points_colored(sx, sy, colour, 5.0)
      .title("All rules at confidence >= 0.8 (darker = higher lift)")
      .x_label("support (share of passengers)")
      .y_label("confidence")
      .size(860, 500)
      .save_svg("build/apriori_rules.svg");
}
```
